Article 34 Where the right to life and health of a citizen is infringed upon, the compensation money shall be calculated according to the following provisions:
(1) If bodily injury is caused, medical expenses, nursing expenses, and compensation for reduced income due to lost working time shall be paid. The daily compensation for reduced income shall be calculated on the basis of the average daily wage of employees in the previous year of the state, with the maximum amount not exceeding five times the average annual wage of employees in the previous year of the state;
(2) If partial or total loss of the ability to work is caused, medical expenses, nursing expenses, expenses for assistive devices for daily living, rehabilitation expenses, and other necessary expenses increased due to the disability and expenses necessary for continuing treatment, as well as disability compensation, shall be paid. The disability compensation shall be determined according to the degree of loss of ability to work and the disability grade provided by the state, with the maximum amount not exceeding twenty times the average annual wage of employees in the previous year of the state. If total loss of the ability to work is caused, living expenses shall also be paid to any person without the ability to work whom the victim supported;
(3) If death is caused, death compensation and funeral expenses shall be paid, the total amount being twenty times the average annual wage of employees in the previous year of the state. Living expenses shall also be paid to any person without the ability to work whom the deceased supported before death.
The living expenses specified in items (2) and (3) of the preceding paragraph shall be paid by reference to the local minimum subsistence guarantee standard. If the person supported is a minor, living expenses shall be paid until the person reaches the age of eighteen; for any other person without the ability to work, living expenses shall be paid until the person's death.

Article 36 Where the property rights of a citizen, legal person, or other organization are infringed upon and damage is caused, the matter shall be dealt with according to the following provisions:
(1) If a fine, penalty, recovery, confiscation of property, or illegal expropriation or requisition of property is imposed, the property shall be returned;
(2) If property is sealed up, seized, or frozen, the sealing, seizure, or freezing shall be lifted; if damage or loss is caused to the property, compensation shall be made in accordance with items (3) and (4) of this Article;
(3) If the property to be returned is damaged, the original condition shall be restored if possible; if restoration is not possible, corresponding compensation money shall be paid according to the extent of the damage;
(4) If the property to be returned is lost, corresponding compensation money shall be paid;
(5) If the property has been auctioned or sold off, the proceeds from the auction or sale shall be paid; if the proceeds from the sale are obviously lower than the value of the property, corresponding compensation money shall be paid;
(6) If a permit or license is revoked, or production or business operation is ordered to cease or suspend, the necessary recurrent expenses during the period of cessation or suspension shall be compensated;
(7) If a fine or penalty already executed is returned, or money recovered or confiscated is returned, or frozen deposits or remittances are unfrozen, interest on deposits at the bank for the same period shall be paid;
(8) If other damage is caused to property rights, compensation shall be given for direct losses.
